#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Gate-2 evidence pack for the from-scratch pass 1-G4F6P1: recipe table, receipt, drops, label check, format block, dry-run PLAN, checks. Usage: python3 data/make_gate2_brief.py"""
import json, re, os
ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); os.chdir(ROOT)
def R(p): return open(p).read() if os.path.exists(p) else f'[missing: {p}]'
rec = json.load(open('data/arms/R4_full/receipt.json'))
parts = ["""Review target: GATE 2 (assembly + launch readiness) for the from-scratch pass 1-G4F6P1 (legacy R4_full). THIRTEENTH pass. Your v12 verdict (docs/reviews/ASTRA_gate2_full_v12_20260915.md): HOLD on V12-H1 (\\left/\\right removed as substrings, so \\leftarrow equalled \\rightarrow); V12-M1 (four MC stems), V12-M2 (S2_00638 invents a divorce), V12-M3 (math_train_3060 explanation), V12-M4 (overlays replaced one occurrence of a repeated id), V12-L1 (global id uniqueness not asserted), V12-L2 (S2_00514 ThessCard completion), V12-L3 (docstring).
Fixes: H1 -> canon() and _norm() remove \\left/\\right only as complete commands (command-boundary regex); regressions: \\leftarrow vs \\rightarrow, a\\leftarrow b vs a\\rightarrow b, \\Leftrightarrow vs \\leftrightarrow disagree; \\left(1\\right) vs (1) and \\left(1,2\\right) vs (1, 2) agree. 152 self-tests. All 12,028 records re-decided (deltas with pairs in §C). M1 -> the four stems banned in the pool (targets and demonstrations); block rebuilt. M2/L2 -> content search over ALL convskills assistant turns: the divorce reply is a shared seed answer in 21 rows, the ThessCard completion answer in 25 rows; all excluded by content (reasons file). Disclosure on this block: 2,259 of its 2,851 rows contain an assistant turn reused in >= 3 rows (554 such turns, up to 40 copies) — reuse is the block's construction, so every defective seed answer found is excluded across all its rows; the owner has been asked whether to keep the block in this pass. M3 -> math_train_3060 excluded. M4 -> personality overlays now replace EVERY occurrence of a repeated id (receipt personality_overlays.occurrences_replaced and personality_overlay_detail per overlay). L1 -> generated #r<k> suffixes are reserved against all existing ids; inherited rows with bare ids reused across configs (e.g. '4788' in three configs) are prefixed with their config like the new blocks (receipt inherited_ids_prefixed_with_config); the assembler asserts global uniqueness over train + dev. L3 -> comparator docstring corrected; the masked-row wording states the decision for this pass.
F1: §I holds the validator inspection AND the training-path audits (a) launch config 4 rows, (b) launch config 40-row cohort from the final manifest, (c) raw-message path on the same cohort with --expect-deficit, (d) negative control (launch config, --expect-deficit, must FAIL). The launch training path is the pretokenized one (validator labels handed to TRL as assistant_masks). No row with a masked turn is in the manifest (decision kept).
"""]
parts.append("\n=== §A RECIPE TABLE (docs/RECIPE_R4_full_20260915.md) ===\n" + R('docs/RECIPE_R4_full_20260915.md'))
parts.append("\n=== §B RECEIPT (data/arms/R4_full/receipt.json) ===\n" + json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)[:20000])
ld = json.load(open('data/math/cut2/final/label_disagreements.json')); parts.append("\n=== §C LABEL CHECK (independent blind solve, medium effort; positive join) ===\n" + json.dumps({k: v for k, v in ld.items() if k not in ('agreed', 'disagree')}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1) + f"\nagreed ids: {len(ld['agreed'])}, disagree ids: {len(ld['disagree'])} (first 20 disagree: {ld['disagree'][:20]})\nper-block label counts from the receipt: {json.dumps(rec.get('label_counts'))}\nwaived (disclosed): {json.dumps(rec.get('waived'))}\nidentities: {json.dumps(rec.get('identities'), indent=1)[:4000]}" + "\nRule: a maths row is kept only where Sol's blind answer agrees with the source label under labelcheck_lib.agree (identity; exact rational equality when either side is number-like; categorical equality; otherwise the exact symbolic fallback equiv_exact; no tolerance anywhere); disagreements and unsolved problems are dropped from BOTH the Greek block and the English GSM8K block. The check is against Sol's medium-effort answer, so a wrong Sol answer drops a good row (cost: coverage), and a wrong label with a matching wrong Sol answer is not caught (bound stated in the ledger).\nSolver script:\n" + R('data/math/cut2/independent_solve.py') + "\nFinalizer:\n" + R('data/math/cut2/finalize_label_check.py') + "\nComparator library (labelcheck_lib.py):\n" + R('data/math/cut2/labelcheck_lib.py') + "\nequiv500 (benchmark comparator, verbatim):\n" + R('data/benchmarks_el/math500/equiv500.py') + "\nFingerprint backfill script:\n" + R('data/math/cut2/backfill_solve_fingerprints.py') + "\nSolve manifest (file-time evidence):\n" + R('data/math/cut2/out/independent_solve.manifest.json') + "\nFinalizer log (self-test count, live/stale/missing, agreement by source and by decision path):\n" + R('results/R4_full/label_check.txt') + "\nLabel-check delta (previous finalization -> this one):\n" + R('results/R4_full/label_check_delta.json') + "\nLabel-check delta vs the v7-reviewed approval set (v7 -> current comparator), with the pairs (results/R4_full/label_check_delta_vs_v7.json + pairs):\n" + R('results/R4_full/label_check_delta_vs_v7.json') + "\n" + R('results/R4_full/label_check_delta_vs_v7_pairs.txt') + "\nHistory: v8.0 (first strict pass) flipped 37 legitimate LaTeX reference forms (45,\\!045; \\frac53; \\frac 79; K=8; -1, 1); v8.1 normalised exactly those forms; v9 removes the remaining float-tolerance route and the list/unit misreadings. Cohort record:\n" + R('results/R4_full/deficit_sample_cohort.json') + "\nExclusions + reasons:\n" + R('data/exclude_rows_r4_reasons.json'))
parts.append("\n=== §D FORMAT BLOCK (data/format_block/receipt.json + builder) ===\n" + R('data/format_block/receipt.json') + "\n" + R('data/format_block/build_mc_fewshot.py') + "\nNOTE (this pass): the builder flags demonstration answers train=false, but the assembler REMOVES the flags because the training path supervises every assistant turn; in the manifest the demonstrations are supervised (correct letters). Three sample rows (builder output):\n" + ''.join(open('data/format_block/mc_fewshot_en.jsonl').readlines()[:3]))
parts.append("\n=== §E ASSEMBLER (data/assemble_full_r4.py, verbatim) ===\n" + R('data/assemble_full_r4.py'))
parts.append("\n=== §F TRAINER DRY-RUN + CONFIG + LAUNCH BINDING (chain excerpt) ===\n" + '\n'.join(l for l in open('cluster/r4_full_chain.sh') if 'sha256' in l or 'expected_train_rows' in l or 'md5' in l) + "\n" + (lambda t: (re.search(r'PLAN (\{.*\})', t).group(1) if re.search(r'PLAN (\{.*\})', t) else '[no PLAN line]') + ('\nDRY_RUN_OK' if 'DRY_RUN_OK' in t else '\nNO OK MARKER'))(R('results/R4_full/dryrun.log')) + "\nConfig:\n" + R('cluster/configs/R4_full.yaml') + "\nPreflight: " + R('results/R4_full/preflight.txt'))
parts.append("\n=== §G PILOT READOUT EXCERPT (why the block is in) ===\n" + R('docs/PILOT_READOUT_20260914.md')[:6000])
parts.append("\n=== §H SAMPLE ROWS FROM THE NEW BLOCKS (5 each: greek_math_v2, math_en_gsm, math_en_math, convskills_v2, format_mc; there is NO correcting block in this pass) ===\n")
import collections; seen = collections.Counter()
for l in open('data/arms/R4_full/train.jsonl'):
    r = json.loads(l); c = r['config']
    if c in ('greek_math_v2', 'math_en_gsm', 'math_en_math', 'convskills_v2', 'format_mc') and seen[c] < 5: seen[c] += 1; parts.append(f"--- {c} {r['id']} (total {sum(len(m['content']) for m in r['messages'])} chars, unclipped)\n" + '\n'.join(f"[{m['role']}{' (unsupervised)' if m.get('train') is False else ''}] {m['content']}" for m in r['messages']) + '\n')
    if sum(seen.values()) >= 25: break
def X(pat, before, n):
    ls = open('cluster/sft_train.py').readlines(); i = next(k for k, l in enumerate(ls) if pat in l); return ''.join(ls[max(0, i - before):i - before + n])
parts.append('\n=== §I TRAINER LABEL INSPECTION (cluster, sft5 env, the trainer\'s tokenize_messages on the launch manifest) ===\n' + R('results/R4_full/labels_inspection.txt') + '\n--- trainer code: tokenize_messages (the validator path; with pretokenized_masks: true these labels ARE the training labels; the raw-message path of rounds 1-3 rebuilt the mask itself and lost supervision after partial-character tokens) ---\n' + X('def tokenize_messages(', 0, 56) + '\n' + X('"packing": True', 8, 14) + '\n--- inspection script (validator path) ---\n' + R('cluster/inspect_labels.py') + '\n--- trainer window check (validate: every row rendered; over max_length fails the dry-run) ---\n' + X('truncation is forbidden', 20, 30) + '\n--- trainer dataset construction (pretokenized rows + assistant_masks when the flag is on) + run ---\n' + X('def _dataset(', 0, 22) + X('def run(config', 0, 26) + '\n=== §I2 TRL TRAINING-PATH LABEL AUDITS (every batch, token by token; exit code) ===\n(a) launch config, 3 manifest rows + emoji conversation (results/R4_full/trl_audit_launch4.txt):\n' + R('results/R4_full/trl_audit_launch4.txt') + '\n(b) launch config, the 40-row exposure cohort drawn from the FINAL manifest (results/R4_full/trl_audit_launch40.txt):\n' + R('results/R4_full/trl_audit_launch40.txt') + '\n(c) raw-message path (rounds 1-3), the same 40 rows, --expect-deficit (results/R4_full/trl_audit_raw40.txt):\n' + R('results/R4_full/trl_audit_raw40.txt') + '\n(d) NEGATIVE CONTROL: launch config, 4 rows, --expect-deficit (must FAIL; results/R4_full/trl_audit_negcontrol.txt):\n' + R('results/R4_full/trl_audit_negcontrol.txt') + '\n--- audit script ---\n' + R('cluster/inspect_trl_labels.py') + '\n=== §I2b TRAINER-PATH DECISION (15 Sept 13:10) ===\nManifest exposure (results/R4_full/byte_fallback_exposure.json; an EXPOSURE count of rows containing partial-character tokens, not a count of rows with faulty labels):\n' + R('results/R4_full/byte_fallback_exposure.json') + '\nDecision: config pretokenized_masks: true -> sft_train._dataset hands TRL input_ids + assistant_masks from tokenize_messages (the validator path) and assistant_only_loss is off (TRL folds assistant_masks into labels; this TRL: docstring lines 853-858). Collator labels under this path: audits (a) and (b). Trainer diff (pretokenized path, default off):\n' + __import__('subprocess').run(['diff', 'data/math/cut2/backup/sft_train.py.pre_pretok', 'cluster/sft_train.py'], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout + '\nNOT yet exercised in a real GPU run (packing + flash-attn on pretokenized rows): the launch is watched from step 0; a failure there costs the queue time only. Rounds 1-3 (incl. the incumbent) were trained with the raw-message path and its deficit (audit (c)).' + '\n=== §I3 RENDERED ROW LENGTHS (results/R4_full/rendered_lengths.json) ===\n' + R('results/R4_full/rendered_lengths.json') + '\n--- script ---\n' + R('cluster/rendered_lengths.py'))
parts.append('\n=== §J S5m AUDIT + PREDECLARED CRITERIA ===\nS5m audit summary: ' + R('data/convskills/v2/audit_s5m_summary.json') + '\n' + (lambda t: t[t.index('**Gate-2 outcome'):] if '**Gate-2 outcome' in t else '')(R('docs/R4_EXEC_PLAN_20260914.md')))
open('docs/reviews/briefs/astra_gate2_full_v13.md', 'w').write(''.join(parts)); print('brief chars', sum(len(x) for x in parts))
